  "claim": "Korematsu v. United States and Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire are both cases regarding the rights of U. S. citizens.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Korematsu v. United States. Sentence: Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214 (1944), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066, which ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps during World War II regardless of citizenship.\nPage: Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire. Sentence: Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.",
