        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Cases: Korematsu v. United States; Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire\n- Organizations: United States Supreme Court\n- Policies: Executive Order 9066\n- Concepts: Japanese American internment; fighting words doctrine; First Amendment freedom of speech\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- In 1942, Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568, was a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine as a limitation on the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.\n- During World War II, Executive Order 9066 ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps regardless of citizenship.\n- In 1944, Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214, was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066.",
